## Research: confirm DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash is real before touching code

WebSearch "DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash model API" and "DeepSeek API model list 2026
deepseek-chat deepseek-reasoner deprecated" -> confirmed a real model exists,
current API model id likely `deepseek-flash`, legacy `deepseek-chat`/
`deepseek-reasoner` on a ~3-month discontinuation clock from a 2026-07-24
DeepSeek announcement.

WebFetch https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing/
-> "deepseek-flash ... Maps to: DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash"

WebFetch https://api-docs.deepseek.com/news/news260910/
-> "Use `deepseek-flash` for the new V4.1-Flash model"; deepseek-chat/
   deepseek-reasoner not mentioned in this release note (confirmed via the
   pricing-page fetch and the model-list search above instead).

Decision: use `deepseek-flash` as the literal API model string everywhere
the code currently hardcodes `deepseek-chat`/`deepseek-reasoner`, not the
display name "DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash" (not a valid API string, same relationship
as any other provider's display name vs. wire model id).

