## VTID allocation (after an initial wrong assumption)

Initially assumed the gateway's VTID allocator was unreachable from this
sandbox and opened PR #3268 without a VTID, citing IF-THEN rule 1/§4.1. The
user (platform owner) pushed back, correctly, that this hadn't actually been
tried.

$ curl -sS -m 15 -X POST "https://gateway.vitanaland.com/api/v1/vtid/allocate" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{"source":"claude-code","layer":"AGTL","module":"LLM_ROUTING"}'
-> 201 {"ok":true,"vtid":"VTID-03816","num":3816,"id":"0c5f3cd4-..."}

$ curl -sS -m 15 "https://gateway.vitanaland.com/api/v1/vtid/VTID-03816"
-> 200 {"ok":true,"data":{"vtid":"VTID-03816","status":"allocated",
   "title":"Claude code","spec_status":"missing", ...}}

Tried (and confirmed do NOT apply / are not usable without a full spec):
  PATCH /api/v1/vtid/VTID-03816                 -> 404 (route doesn't exist)
  PATCH /api/v1/specs/:vtid                      -> requires an existing
                                                     spec_current_id (none
                                                     exists for a freshly
                                                     allocated shell row)
  POST /api/v1/vtid/lifecycle/start              -> gated on
                                                     spec_status='approved'
                                                     already (409
                                                     SPEC_NOT_APPROVED
                                                     otherwise) — read the
                                                     handler source in
                                                     services/gateway/src/
                                                     routes/events.ts rather
                                                     than probing it live
  POST /api/v1/specs/:vtid/approve               -> gated on spec_status
                                                     already being
                                                     'quality_checked' or
                                                     'validated' — same
                                                     read-the-source
                                                     confirmation, not a
                                                     live probe (this route
                                                     mutates ledger state,
                                                     so it was not
                                                     exercised speculatively
                                                     against production)

Decision: use VTID-03816 as allocated (real, ledger row exists) without
forcing the ledger's status/spec_status fields through the full spec
pipeline retroactively for already-shipped, already-tested work — see the
PR body and CLAUDE.md changelog entry for the reasoning.

$ curl -sS -m 15 -X PATCH "https://gateway.vitanaland.com/api/v1/vtid/VTID-03816" ...
-> (attempted before discovering it's not a real route — see above)
